==Strategy==
A tip is to stop using the [[Cat Cannon]] once Dober P.D spawns, you'll need it to kill the Assassin Bear when it appears. If you have [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Driller Cat]], you can stack two on the first THE SLOTH, and then they can perma-[[Weaken|weaken]] the R.Ost and the Dober P.D. However, be wary of Dober's waves, as they will still be able to hurt the Drillers. In general, use meatshields, anti-Wave Cats, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. However, if you have an Uber that has better DPS and range than either of those, or is [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]], you can replace one of them with said Uber.

This stage has an enemy limit of 1, meaning that unless the previous threats are down, more would not spawn. Therefore, it is possible to also [[cheese]] the stage with Long Distance units if Anti-Traitless crowd controllers are stacked and used to knock THE SLOTH/R.Ost all the way back to the base.

==='''Strategy 1 (Cheese, 1-3 crown)'''===
{{Lineup
|Sexy Legs Cat
|Crazed Gross Cat
|Creepmallow
|Cat O'Lantern
|Golfer Cat|30
|Tourist Cat|30
}}

'''Battle:''' Start the battle by letting THE SLOTH get close to your base while you upgrade the [[Worker Cat]], and when it's around 3/4ths across the battlefield, start sending out Tourist Cats. THE SLOTH will attack a few times, but Tourist has enough health to tank its hits until you can send out a second, and at this point THE SLOTH should be permafrozen and pinned against the enemy base. Once the Tourist Cats start clipping through, start sending out Golfer Cats, they will slowly clip through THE SLOTH and start hitting the base. Keep sending out more Golfers like this until you win.

==Trivia==
*This stage's name is in German. It means ballpoint pen, although it should be "Kugelschreiber", with no space in between.

